---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SimHero from '../../../components/SimHero.jsx';
import {PARAMETER_REGISTER,LIMITATIONS,MODEL_VERSION,BUDGET} from '../../../lib/axon-interface/settings.mjs';
import {MRG_PARAMETERS} from '../../../lib/axon-interface/mrg.mjs';
import {FIELD_PARAMETERS} from '../../../lib/axon-interface/field.mjs';
import {references} from '../../../lib/axon-interface/evidence.mjs';
import mrg from '../../../../docs/axon-interface/mrg-numerical-report.json';
import field from '../../../../docs/axon-interface/field-validation.json';
import coupled from '../../../../docs/axon-interface/mrg-coupled-report.json';
import integration from '../../../../docs/axon-interface/integration-validation.json';
import reproduction from '../../../../docs/axon-interface/reproduction-report.json';
import '../../../styles/axon-interface.css';
const f=n=>n==null?'—':typeof n==='boolean'?String(n):typeof n==='number'?(n!==0&&Math.abs(n)<.0001?n.toExponential(5):n.toLocaleString('en-US',{maximumFractionDigits:8})):typeof n==='object'?JSON.stringify(n):String(n);
const gaps=[
 ['Spiral-ganglion replacement mechanism','Not implemented','The straight MRG motor-fiber cohort and optional central load do not instantiate distinct peripheral, pre-somatic, somatic, post-somatic and central structures.'],
 ['Soma-in-well addressing','Not implemented','Sources lie outside the fascicle. Individual insulating wells, contacts, apertures and aperture resistance are not resolved.'],
 ['Architecture-matched controls','Partly applicable','Zero drive, isolation and local/whole-cell silencing run. Junction block is N/A for a projecting-neuron architecture; postoperative no-construct preservation is not calculated.'],
 ['Original-host denominator and continuity','Not modeled','The electrical cohort contains synthetic identities. It has no original preoperative population or postoperative target-continuity experiment.'],
 ['MRG membrane numerical verification',mrg.summary.numericalGatePassed?'Passed at declared fixtures':'Not passed',mrg.summary.requiredPass+' required checks passed; '+mrg.summary.requiredFail+' failed. Historical failures remain visible.'],
 ['Anisotropic field numerical verification',field.results.every(r=>r.status==='pass')?'Passed at declared fixtures':'Not passed',field.results.filter(r=>r.status==='pass').length+' field checks passed.'],
 ['Published diameter–velocity relation','Not established','Broad class-band diagnostics do not independently calibrate a species-specific physiological relation.'],
 ['Complete Stage 1','Incomplete','A verified conditional ganglion and well model is still needed. Uncertain parameters may be exposed as hypothetical and tested; the missing mechanisms are not merely a lack of human calibration.']
];
---
<Layout pageTitle="Axon-Resolution Laboratory · Methods & Validation" description="Equations, frozen numerical gates, parameter provenance and retained failures." wide compactHeader>
<div class="ax-lab ax-methods">
<SimHero kicker="Axon resolution / Methods and evidence" title="A traceable electrical core" intro="What this calculation establishes, what failed, and what remains uncalculated." links={[{href:'/simulations/biohybrid-axon-interface/',label:'Open laboratory'},{href:'/simulations/biohybrid-axon-interface/questions/',label:'Scientific questions'},{href:'/simulations/biohybrid-axon-interface/validation.json',label:'Numerical report JSON'}]}/>
<div class="ax-boundary"><span class="ax-kicker">Release status</span><p><strong>Development candidate with numerical components tested at declared fixtures.</strong> The complete requested Stage 1 biohybrid ganglion-replacement model is not yet implemented. Numerical agreement does not validate biological prediction.</p></div>
<section id="scope"><h2>01 · Model scope and release gates</h2><p>This laboratory resolves a synthetic one-fascicle cohort. Each cell is a double-cable myelinated axon with optional hypothetical central loading. Every stated cell is calculated at the requested resolution; there is no threshold screening or extrapolation to a full human nerve. The electrical clock is milliseconds. Growth and chronic-response models belong to later stages.</p><div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>{gaps.map(([a,b,c])=><tr><td>{a}</td><td>{b}</td><td>{c}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>The prompt permits estimated and hypothetical parameters when exposed and subjected to sensitivity studies. That permits a conditional architecture; it does not permit an absent mechanism to be counted as a successful one.</p></section>
<section><h2>02 · Identities, census and addressability</h2><pre>Original-host endpoint:
Y_axon = N(original, continuous, uniquely recruited, mechanism-dependent) / N_original

Electrical-cohort endpoint:
Y_model = N(exclusively recruited modeled outputs) / N_resolved

R[k,i] = 1 only if the named isolated channel evokes
three ordered upward 0 mV crossings on consecutive distal nodes.</pre><p>The original-host ratio is <strong>not modeled</strong> here. A hypothetical complete ganglion replacement would remove original neuronal identities, giving zero original-host preservation by definition. New engineered axons cannot be renamed as original identities. That architectural statement is separate from calculated electrical selectivity.</p><p>An output is electrically exclusive only when an isolated matrix row contains exactly that output. Shared rows retain their full co-recruited sets. Loss during local conductance removal is local dependence, not proof of synaptic mediation. Conditional local-initiation evidence additionally requires the earliest observed crossings to lie within the silenced region.</p><p>Matrix rank is a linear-algebra descriptor; it does not establish nonlinear controllability. The information diagnostic is deterministic activation-pattern entropy under a uniform prior over isolated named channels at one amplitude, not an experimentally estimated communication capacity.</p></section>
<section><h2>03 · Myelinated double cable at 37 °C</h2><p>The MRG formulation follows the original ModelDB source pinned to commit <code>b15daeda6ea368df0198d257f339cf5e840cf31c</code>. Nodes carry transient and persistent sodium, slow potassium and leak. MYSA, FLUT and STIN regions retain distinct geometry, passive membranes, periaxonal spaces, and myelin capacitance and conductance. Diameter selects published tabulated geometry; unsupported interpolation is rejected.</p><pre>V_m = V_intracellular − V_periaxonal
V_periaxonal,absolute = w + φ_e
I_m = C_m dV_m/dt + I_Naf + I_Nap + I_Ks + I_leak
I_myelin = C_my d(w)/dt + G_my w

Intracellular and periaxonal axial-current balances are solved together.
Applied extracellular voltage enters differences between connected compartments.
Electrode current is not substituted for intracellular current injection.</pre><p>A block-tridiagonal solve advances the coupled cable. The reference model equilibrates for 20 ms before the observed window. Every intervention starts from the same equilibrated state; only the named conductances or drive change. Drift is recorded without correcting a leak reversal or clipping voltage.</p><p>The production benchmark uses 1.25 µs steps and three numerical segments per passive section. Eleven nodes resolve 311 compartments. The original one-segment discretization and larger steps remain as retained convergence failures.</p><p>Enlarging a node into a soma and assigning full MRG nodal kinetics generated spontaneous firing. The passive 20 µm central compartment is a separate hypothetical load experiment. A passing passive variant does not erase the active-soma failure or establish spiral-ganglion physiology.</p></section>
<section><h2>04 · Anisotropic finite-element conductor</h2><pre>∇ · (Σ ∇φ) = −q
Σ_endoneurium = diag(σ_transverse, σ_transverse, σ_longitudinal)
K_ab = element volume × (∇N_a)ᵀ Σ (∇N_b)
K φ_k = b_source,k − b_return,k
φ(t) = Σ_k I_k(t) φ_k

Reciprocal neural voltage:
V_record = Σ_i T_record,i I_outer,i
I_outer [nA] × T [mV/µA] gives recording [µV].</pre><p>Conforming P1 tetrahedra resolve endoneurium, perineurium, epineurium and surrounding conductor. The default component mesh has 21,349 vertices and 120,960 tetrahedra, with two radial elements across the 15 µm perineurium. The outer cylinder and ends are grounded. This is a finite-domain calculation; production boundary truncation is not established by the analytic-boundary benchmarks.</p><p>Each channel uses a Gaussian volumetric source and matching opposite sink, integrated at fixed physical Gauss–Hermite quadrature points into the P1 basis. The finite-source radius is three standard deviations. It is separate from physical metal contact area. Underresolved, outside, overlapping or incompatible source supports cause visible errors.</p><p>True residual, current closure and source–return imbalance are reported. Superposition and reciprocity are checked. The perineurium is ohmic; frequency dispersion and capacitance are absent. Conductivities are preparation-dependent estimated inputs, not measured human 37 °C values.</p><p>Well-wall insulation, aperture resistance and metal/electrolyte impedance are absent. The geometric capacity and Poisson occupancy diagnostics make no shielding or survival claim.</p></section>
<section><h2>05 · Matched interventions and source partition</h2><p>Assigned, locally silenced and whole-cell-silenced cases retain morphology, temperature, field coefficients, initial state, step and observation window. Local silencing removes active conductances at the central node and its two immediate nodal neighbors, retaining distal excitability. Whole-cell silencing removes active conductances everywhere and cannot distinguish soma drive from direct excitation of that same cell’s axon.</p><p>Zero-drive and zero-drive silencing checks detect spontaneous or intervention-induced activity. Every row is a channel-isolation experiment. No junction is invented: junction block is not applicable. Postoperative no-construct preservation is not modeled; a zero-drive cable is not an empty-conduit repair comparator.</p><p>Recordings use current entering the volume conductor, including nodal discharge and myelin/periaxonal bookkeeping. Raw internodal axolemmal current is not all assigned directly to extracellular space. Model-source voltage, host-source voltage, imposed artifact and instantaneous sum are separate exports. Host sources are zero because no separate host population is instantiated.</p><p>The artifact at a saved state uses the same preceding solver-step average as the saved membrane currents; explicit interval start and end times are exported. This is a known-source partition, not an inverse reconstruction or spike-sorting result. Instantaneous waveforms add; peak-to-peak amplitudes do not.</p></section>
<section id="parameters"><h2>06 · Parameter register</h2><p>Every control has one evidence class. Model constants do not become fits to engineered organoid cells. Derived field settings and all physical coordinates are exported.</p><div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Default</th><th>Units</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>{PARAMETER_REGISTER.map(p=><tr><td><code>{p.key}</code></td><td>{f(p.default)}</td><td>{p.units}</td><td>{p.evidence}</td><td>{p.provenance}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><details class="ax-inspection"><summary>MRG constants and definitions</summary><div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th><th>Units</th><th>Evidence / source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(MRG_PARAMETERS).map(([key,p])=><tr><td>{key}</td><td><code>{f(p.value)}</code></td><td>{p.units}</td><td>{p.evidence} · {p.source}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details><details class="ax-inspection"><summary>Field component defaults</summary><div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th><th>Units</th><th>Evidence / source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{FIELD_PARAMETERS.map(p=><tr><td>{p.key}</td><td>{f(p.default)}</td><td>{p.units}</td><td>{p.evidence} · {p.provenance}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details></section>
<section id="validation"><h2>07 · Frozen acceptance and numerical results</h2><p>Acceptance thresholds precede the studies and are not relaxed to obtain a pass. Comparisons use identical observation times without shifts, baseline correction or amplitude rescaling. Each row applies to a declared fixture, not every possible setting.</p><h3>MRG double cable</h3><div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Measured</th><th>Limit</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{mrg.tests.map(t=><tr><td>{t.name}{t.required===false?' · retained diagnostic':''}</td><td>{f(t.measured)} {t.unit}</td><td>{f(t.limit)}</td><td>{t.status}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><h3>Volume conductor</h3><div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Measured</th><th>Limit</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{field.results.map(t=><tr><td>{t.name}</td><td>{f(t.value)}</td><td>{f(t.tolerance)}</td><td>{t.status}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>Native NEURON uses its own cable solver and compiled original channel mechanism. Python independently rebuilds gradients, stiffness, Gaussian quadrature and interpolation, then solves with scipy; it does not import the JavaScript stiffness. Same-discretization agreement is separate from refinement and analytic verification.</p><p>The homogeneous benchmark applies the infinite-medium analytic solution at the finite boundary and samples outside source support. The layered-cylinder benchmark applies its radial analytic boundary conditions. These checks verify representable cases; they do not establish negligible error from the grounded production boundary.</p></section>
<section><h2>Published physiological relation remains separate</h2><p>The broad class velocity bands are diagnostics. They do not establish the published diameter relation. Measurements use 41 nodes and monitor locations away from initiation and sealed ends. The cited large-cat-fiber line is 5.66 m/s per µm. No post hoc tolerance or hidden channel retuning is introduced.</p><div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Diameter</th><th>Calculated velocity</th><th>Published cat-line value</th><th>Difference</th></tr></thead><tbody>{(mrg.conductionLiteratureComparison??[]).map(c=><tr><td>{c.fiberDiameterUm} µm</td><td>{f(c.measuredVelocityMps)} m/s</td><td>{f(c.literatureLineMps)} m/s</td><td>{f(100*c.fractionalDifference)}%</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p><a href="https://journals.physiology.org/doi/full/10.1152/jn.00353.2001">MRG Figure 8 and its cited physiological comparison</a> concern a specific preparation. Native-solver agreement does not calibrate human ganglion physiology. The published diameter relation remains unvalidated.</p></section>
<section><h2>Production field → native membrane reference</h2><p>The coupled comparison uses actual production FEM coefficients, the first seeded cell, all 311 compartments, 1.25 µs steps and a declared 1,000 µA stress stimulus. The native reference receives identical applied extracellular voltages and initial conditions. This is a numerical stress fixture, not a recommended implant operating point.</p><div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Intervention</th><th>Worst-node RMS / mV</th><th>Maximum recording error / µV</th><th>Crossings JS / NEURON</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{coupled.rows.map(r=><tr><td>{r.intervention}</td><td>{f(r.membraneMaxNodeRmsMv)}</td><td>{f(r.maxRecordingErrorUv)}</td><td>{r.jsCrossings} / {r.neuronCrossings}</td><td>{r.status}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><h3>Software and reproduction</h3><p>{integration.summary.passed} software checks passed, {integration.summary.failed} failed and {integration.summary.skipped} were skipped. Checks cover deterministic replay, production workers, cancellation, request identities, malformed inputs, work budgets, control metadata and export integrity.</p><div class="ax-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Reproduction stage</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{reproduction.stages.map(s=><tr><td>{s.name}</td><td>{s.status}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>Overall reproduction status: <strong>{reproduction.status}</strong>. The report records commands, runtime, hardware and source hashes. A source change during verification invalidates that run, even if its numerical stages pass.</p></section>
<section id="failures"><h2>08 · Retained failures</h2><p>Original failed measurements remain visible with their cause and correction. A different passing model does not convert the failed one into a pass.</p>{mrg.retainedFailures.map(x=><article class="ax-control-card is-failed"><h3>{x.id??'Retained membrane failure'}</h3><p>{x.cause??x.description}</p><pre>{JSON.stringify(x,null,2)}</pre></article>)}<p>The initial field radial-refinement discrepancy was <strong>19.58%</strong> against the unchanged 10% gate. Physical-space source integration and a refined surrounding-region mesh reduced it to about 2.45%. The historical result is retained with its recovery provenance; the current report contains a fresh execution.</p><p>An execution-environment reset interrupted development before the first source checkpoint. Exact field and protocol sources were recovered by their hashes; the membrane source was reconstructed from the pinned reference. Current passing reports require fresh verification of the recovered revision. Historical results are not relabeled as evidence for changed source.</p></section>
<section><h2>09 · Reproduction, budgets and exports</h2><p>Executable verification, pinned dependencies, original reference sources, tolerances and numerical reports live under <code>scripts/axon-interface/</code> and <code>docs/axon-interface/</code>. Reproduction executes independent solvers, not stored pass flags.</p><pre>python3 scripts/axon-interface/reproduce.py
node --test tests/axon-interface-contracts.mjs
node scripts/verify-axon-interface-build.mjs</pre><p>Model version: <code>{MODEL_VERSION}</code>. Caps include {BUDGET.maxCableSolves.toLocaleString('en-US')} cable solves, {BUDGET.maxCompartmentSteps.toLocaleString('en-US')} compartment steps and {BUDGET.maxSavedValues.toLocaleString('en-US')} scalar values. Over-budget requests fail before solving. Neither resolution nor census is silently reduced.</p><p>Solves run in a Web Worker. Cancellation terminates the worker; request identities prevent late results from replacing newer requests. Changing controls preserves completed settings. JSON contains units, versions, identities, geometry, every intervention, sampled traces and limitations. CSV separates recruitment, per-axon events, yield cascade and source time series.</p></section>
<section><h2>10 · Standing limitations</h2><ul>{LIMITATIONS.map(x=><li>{x}</li>)}</ul><p>The next architecture requires explicit bipolar morphology, well/aperture field boundaries, original identities and a no-construct comparator, with sensitivity to every hypothetical parameter. Oxygen transport, growth, chronic response, full-census screening and additional modalities belong to later stages.</p></section>
<section id="references"><h2>Primary reference register</h2><ol class="ax-reference-list">{references.map(r=><li id={r.id}><span class="ax-evidence">{r.evidence}</span><br/><a href={r.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{r.title}</a><small>{r.scope}</small></li>)}</ol></section>
</div></Layout>

